      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case of CAA in a 68-year-old male patient is reported. The patient had vague abdominal pain for 1 year. Physical examination revealed a pulsatile abdominal mass on the epigastrium. Abdominal ultrasonography and visceral arteriography confirmed the diagnosis of CAA. Aneurysmectomy with direct implantation was performed transabdominally."},
